@MKISTM  I have cmake build configuration and the warning has nothing to do with IDE. 

The warning comes from these compilation flags:
`add_compile_options(-Wall -Wextra -Wpedantic)`

Hi @vilesovds,

Our development teams confirmed the issue you pointed out.  As a fix, they propose you to add the else case described above :
```
  else
  {
    /* Update ADC state machine to error */
    SET_BIT(hadc->State, HAL_ADC_STATE_ERROR_INTERNAL);
    
    /* Set ADC error code to ADC IP internal error */
    SET_BIT(hadc->ErrorCode, HAL_ADC_ERROR_INTERNAL);
  }

```
 in the following functions : 

- ` HAL_ADC_Start()` line [805](https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/stm32f2xx_hal_driver/blob/6e95e5668f6a8900ecb073db847ff71898bde799/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_adc.c#L805)

- `HAL_ADC_Start_IT()` line [1099](https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/stm32f2xx_hal_driver/blob/6e95e5668f6a8900ecb073db847ff71898bde799/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_adc.c#L1099)
- `HAL_ADC_Start_DMA()` line [1419 ](https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/stm32f2xx_hal_driver/blob/6e95e5668f6a8900ecb073db847ff71898bde799/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_adc.c#L1419)
- `HAL_ADCEx_InjectedStart()` line [205](https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/stm32f2xx_hal_driver/blob/6e95e5668f6a8900ecb073db847ff71898bde799/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_adc_ex.c#L225)

- `HAL_ADCEx_InjectedStart_IT()` line [317](https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/stm32f2xx_hal_driver/blob/6e95e5668f6a8900ecb073db847ff71898bde799/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_adc_ex.c#L317)

- ` HAL_ADCEx_MultiModeStart_DMA()` line [670 ](https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/stm32f2xx_hal_driver/blob/6e95e5668f6a8900ecb073db847ff71898bde799/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_adc_ex.c#L670)


This will be fixed and made available in a future firmware package release. Thank you once more for your contribution. 


With regards,
